review-rounds: 1 (of the analysis that produced this slice, not of this diff)
verdicts: SOUND WITH CORRECTIONS

An independent reviewer assessed the analysis behind this slice and returned SOUND WITH
CORRECTIONS. It confirmed the framing and forgery findings, found stronger in-repo
evidence than the author had (bin/hacktui-mcp-smoke hangs), settled that the 2024-11-05
revision required newline framing so the claim needed no softening, and corrected four
errors: an output reported but not observed, an unverified claim called "decisive", an
overstated double-approval claim, and an omission -- masking absent from the MCP path,
which is now F3 of this slice.

Asserts: gates passed -- test 7 held (152 tests), credo 77 held, dialyzer 43 held,
deps.audit 13 -> 12. Framing, forgery rejection and masking are all covered by tests
that run the real binary.

Does NOT assert: that any reviewer examined THIS diff. None has. Nor that the MCP
server is secure -- it still has no authentication, no per-call audit, and PrivacyMask
remains too narrow to rely on. See BACKLOG.md.
